[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4689748425","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120224#issuecomment-4689748425","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120224","id":4689748425,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABF4fhyQ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-12T09:41:00Z","updated_at":"2026-06-12T09:41:00Z","body":"Can you please explain what issues you have run into with normal configurations from this? I don't see the benefit to the engine of these","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4689748425/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4690343424","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120224#issuecomment-4690343424","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120224","id":4690343424,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABF5D2AA","user":{"login":"mgambrell","id":13956755,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTU2NzU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13956755?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgambrell","html_url":"https://github.com/mgambrell","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgambrell/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgambrell/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgambrell/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgambrell/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgambrell/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgambrell/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgambrell/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgambrell/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgambrell/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-12T10:39:51Z","updated_at":"2026-06-12T10:39:51Z","body":"I'm porting to game consoles. Those aren't normal configurations. \r\n\r\nThere's a hardly-abnormal scenario which is an argument for the _CRT_SECURE_NO_WARNINGS: suppose someone decides to harden the diagnostics because they want to ship a hardened game; or perhaps they are linking other new stuff which hasn't been vetted as much and benefits from hardening. The macro redefinition becomes an error. Or else becomes a new warning which wasn't there before. Reducing noisy warnings benefits the engine by focusing attention on genuine warnings.\r\n\r\nHere's another argument: the codebase has 18 instances of guarded _CRT_SECURE_NO_WARNINGS, in these libraries: embree, glslang, minizip, zlib, zsdt, msdfgen, openxr, vhacd, and sdl. There are 4 instances of unguarded _CRT_SECURE_NO_WARNINGS: 3 in libktx and 1 in godot itself. Whatever benefits accrue to those majorities of libraries from this accrue to godot as well.\r\n\r\nAs for the y-flipping patch: whatever it is that made windows need to control the y-flipping could apply somewhere else... it's governed by glwindow.flipped_y which is governed by EGL_ANGLE_surface_orientation which comes from google, not microsoft. It's a generic concept. Google says it helps improve performance (by saving a final flip). \r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4690343424/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4690367579","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120224#issuecomment-4690367579","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120224","id":4690367579,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABF5FUWw","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-12T10:42:06Z","updated_at":"2026-06-12T10:42:06Z","body":"> Here's another argument: the codebase has 18 instances of guarded _CRT_SECURE_NO_WARNINGS\r\n\r\nThat's a good argument, that makes sense (would have made a great argument in the PR description)\r\n\r\nFor the latter it seems like something to handle in any custom setups, I don't know that it is relevant to the engine as is, but would be for the rendering team to weigh in on","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4690367579/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]